Test fixtures
=============

native-preparation.json records SHA-256 hashes of all 295 files produced
by the original native source preparation recipes. Only CRLF line endings
are normalized to LF. The Node preparation test checks both the file list
and every hash, including source patches, encodings and numeric tables.

ui-before-classes.json contains 1,323 workflow snapshots. Tests account for
changes to format labels, supported picture modes and receive controls.
Waveform and decoded-image behavior are checked separately.

SSTV alignment
--------------

martin2-alignment.wav is the supplied Martin_2_bond.wav recording: mono,
11,025 Hz, 60.797 seconds.
SHA-256: 21e290f85943984b85bcf502ddaa1364413d7434510bd6fe78e1fe743b639c13

The Martin 2 reference image is 320 by 256 RGBA pixels. Receiver settings
use wide band-pass filtering, Hilbert detection, normal sensitivity,
automatic line alignment and no automatic clock-slant correction.
Reference RGBA SHA-256:
    1c8dd0da146b7be490366ed3350cf47cccf20b7d3728d8902b9cb7e4824288dd
Explicit Martin 2 selection starts before the VIS header and produces:
    42e06c400767df7aa0a30d4b26695d538b31ece86027d71b08618273925003f4
Reference WASM SHA-256:
    99c1cde1f10d8d5d0aba9a85d490413eadc5a403cfccbc0d8f50b960b84a2615

Desktop SCAMP recordings
------------------------

scampook-desktop.wav and scfskfst-desktop.wav are unmodified fldigi desktop
transmissions supplied on 2026-10-16. Both are mono 8,000 Hz 16-bit PCM,
centered at 1,000 Hz. The desktop release was not recorded. Expected text
is SCAMPOOK TEST and SCFSKFST TEST; output may also contain the end marker.

scampook-desktop.wav: 21.102 seconds
    e9526a08a9e6fbc5c4a93798eb799366febeee5b910f993c9f2a1f1bf3e30ab0
scfskfst-desktop.wav: 6.840 seconds
    25c99f5935a163254f2c97124f44b3fa7b7e97ae33dae5c463fc180753c61ce7

Desktop fldigi pictures
----------------------

fldigi-picture-*.wav are unmodified mono 8,000 Hz PCM recordings from
fldigi 4.2.13. Tests tune to 1,500 Hz, disable AFC and squelch, and append
five seconds of silence. These fixtures exercise independent desktop
transmissions. SHA-256 hashes:

fldigi-picture-mfsk16.wav: MFSK16, 32 by 24 color
    5906ce320aeaf3cc30a674456a6eae8089850b781c15f7d5d93a070d402790fd
fldigi-picture-thor16.wav: THOR16, 59 by 74 color
    cf4a794ee3d32a7c5153a7957dc3ecb2095c52ff6afe9eff3d5cfcf2dcdaf1d2
fldigi-picture-thor25.wav: THOR25, 59 by 74 color
    de1c02dc69e4f16fe80c545b1bd9c707cc6d8413d903bc55b5a186525362e2b8
fldigi-picture-ifkp.wav: IFKP 1.0x, 160 by 120 color
    ae7d0cae6b95573842bb41f527e45a16427ac6811cb0c89ee3eb3e9e6be5ad60
fldigi-picture-fsq160.wav: FSQ-3, W1TEST sender, 160 by 120 color
    85b4a5d687387303900a197b7cf15c2aba62931f10473f0a852fed404abc0621
fldigi-picture-fsq320.wav: FSQ-3, W1TEST sender, 320 by 240 color
    512d9215f0076bffbfa3717263393f8222612a78891476edc339aa67585cd97f
fldigi-picture-fsq-empty-sender.wav: FSQ-3, no picture expected
    f9ae03287dc697ff1ac03b0e270ae6c49644ec0ebdce555455ab6355f32c5ccb

Browser FSQ photograph
----------------------

fsq-browser-picture.wav is a supplied FSQ-3 transmission: sender TEST,
320 by 240 color, mono 12 kHz 16-bit PCM, 2,443,528 samples. It includes
the 200-sample browser preroll. The source PNG is 320 by 256 pixels.

fsq-browser-picture-expected.rgb stores packed RGB reference pixels.
The source was resized to 300 by 240 using Pillow bilinear resampling
and centered on a white 320 by 240 canvas. Tests allow mean error below
4/255 for FM filtering and resampling differences, with no fitted phase
or spatial alignment. SHA-256 hashes:

fsq-browser-picture.wav:
    104aec042a50565dc7e6eb42a1a92452dcce0fd9760f3fbf1b342a1178455c58
fsq-browser-picture-source.png:
    bd7ec7c6d8cccefee85e010d04d2c434fb325c488e6c2298418b7c2d944b7ecf
fsq-browser-picture-expected.rgb:
    3e0d370a27d5e008ac44f26d27efd4af47d0f1ddb0ef985141680662f2cf9bc8
